Author: Muhammad Sakhawat <muhammadsakhawat@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 21 02:02:17 2026 -0400

    fix(realtime): repair peers left silent by the media-acquisition race
    
    A peer that answered before its own getUserMedia resolved holds no senders and is
    permanently mute to the far side — connected, in the roster, and unrecoverable,
    because setCameraEnabled only flips `enabled` on tracks that already exist and
    replaceTrack needs a sender to replace. That is the one-way media defect: one
    side sees the other perfectly, the other sees nothing, and toggling the camera
    changes nothing.
    
    An earlier attempt at this shipped and broke both sides of live meetings, because
    it used "peer has zero senders" as a proxy for "peer is stale". That predicate is
    invalid: a fresh answerer legitimately has zero senders until handleRemoteOffer
    attaches them, and mutating one mid-negotiation misaligns m-lines. This version
    distinguishes the two from live WebRTC state — remote description applied,
    signalling stable, no offer in flight, media acquisition settled, senders
    genuinely missing — and re-checks eligibility per peer immediately before
    touching anything.
    
    The trigger is the existing heartbeat, and the join path is deliberately NOT
    used: at join the transitional and the broken peer are indistinguishable, which
    is exactly what broke production. By heartbeat time negotiation has settled.
    Worst case is one beat of silence rather than a permanently dead call. The sweep
    is unawaited so presence never waits on repair, and signalling stays in the
    controller — the media layer reports what it repaired, the same division
    startScreenShare() already uses.
    
    Proven locally before shipping, in two real browser participants with real
    getUserMedia and real negotiation. The race was reproduced (offer received with
    localMedia=false, answer sent with zero tracks, far side receiving nothing), then
    nothing was invoked by hand:
    
      beats=2  verdict=waitMedia  senders=0  autoRepairs=0   transitional, untouched
      beats=3  verdict=repair     senders=0  autoRepairs=0   eligible, awaiting beat
      beats=4  verdict=healthy    senders=2  autoRepairs=1   repaired automatically
    
    and the far side recovered video and audio with no user action. Twelve further
    beats left autoRepairs at 1. Camera and mic held OFF across three beats never
    read as missing senders — sender count stayed 2 and the verdict stayed healthy.
    
    The harness is a separate entrypoint, unreachable from lib/main.dart and
    therefore absent from the release bundle. It is committed as evidence, not as
    product.
    
    NOT included, and still open: camera-off/black-frame presentation, refresh
    continuity, firstKeyFromMedia(), meeting-file behaviour. makingOffer remains
    unit-proven and not live-captured; TURN/relay and production-scale multi-peer
    were not certified by this proof.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

